# Line coverage of the workspace, ratcheted: this number may go UP, never
# down (`scripts:V28`, `scripts:C14`). `sherd coverage --check` runs
# `cargo llvm-cov --workspace --all-features --summary-only` and compares
# its TOTAL line percentage with the `lines` row below; `sherd coverage
# --record` raises the row to a new measurement and refuses to lower it.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-27 at adoption (`scripts:T36`): 97.25% lines, 95.99%
# regions, 95.65% functions, over every crate in the workspace -- the
# language crates included, unlike `.lint-debt`, whose ratio reads `src/`
# alone. Two runs of the same tree reported 97.25 both times, so the floor
# starts AT the measurement: a floor below it would let the first real
# drop through unannounced.
#
# A drop is recorded by hand, here, with its reason -- never by editing the
# number alone. A percentage cannot tell a test that asserts from one that
# merely executes; a test written to move this number and asserting
# nothing is the drop it hides, not a fix for it.
lines 97.25
